# Who reviews what, by module.
#
# The modules are the ones CONTRIBUTING.md lists under "Where things live", in
# that order, so a reader comparing the two sees the same division twice rather
# than two that have drifted apart.
#
# Every line names the same person today. That is a fact about who merges, not
# a structure pretending to be one — but the lines are per module on purpose:
# handing one over is then a one-line edit, and the file says which line.
#
# A module is handed over when someone has sent enough changes to it to have
# opinions about where it should go. Sending those changes is how it happens;
# asking first is not.
#
# Language plugins are not here. They live in the `extensions` repository and
# ship as wasm components through its catalog, so this file cannot name their
# owners — that repository's own CODEOWNERS is where they belong.

# Anything no rule below claims.
*                                   @wangyingsm

# Engine — storage, cache, computation, the public API.
/crates/dr-strange-core/            @wangyingsm

# Query language — the openCypher subset.
/crates/dr-strange-parser/          @wangyingsm

# CLI — `drsg` itself, including the agent verbs.
/crates/dr-strange-cli/             @wangyingsm

# MCP server.
/crates/dr-strange-mcp/             @wangyingsm

# Web — JSON-RPC backend, dashboard, change feed.
/crates/dr-strange-web/             @wangyingsm

# LLM — embeddings, digestion, entity resolution, `ask`.
/crates/dr-strange-llm/             @wangyingsm

# Network — outbound proxy policy, shared by every requesting crate.
/crates/dr-strange-net/             @wangyingsm

# Logging — tracing setup for the binaries.
/crates/dr-strange-log/             @wangyingsm

# Python binding — PyO3, published as `drsg-embedded`.
/crates/dr-strange-py/              @wangyingsm

# SDKs — six clients over the JSON-RPC surface.
/sdk/                               @wangyingsm

# Docs — the mdBook, both editions.
/docs/                              @wangyingsm

# Benchmarks — engine comparison, accuracy, token cost.
/benchmarks/                        @wangyingsm

# The gate and the release path. A change here changes what every other
# module is held to, so it is reviewed as its own module.
/.github/                           @wangyingsm
/justfile                           @wangyingsm
/deny.toml                          @wangyingsm
/scripts/                           @wangyingsm
